<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan raises single foreign fund ceiling.</title>
<headline>Taiwan raises single foreign fund ceiling.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Securities and Exchange Commission said on Thursday it has raised the investment ceiling for individual foreign funds in the local stock market to US$600 million from the current $400 million, effective immediately.</p>
<p>Foreign funds can apply for additional entries after reaching the allowed ceiling on a case-by-case basis, an official at the securities watchdog body said.</p>
<p>But foreign funds are required to remit into Taiwan all of the approved $600 million, 70 percent of which must be invested in stocks, the official said.</p>
<p>The central bank has eased restrictions on foreign ownership of local stocks, raising the cap to 25 percent from 15 percent at the beginning of 1996.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
